**Largest unresolved evidence gap: the two ends of the article both rest on evidence that does not hold at full strength.**

- **`CLM-12` — the Riyadh tiebreaker.** The dry-mouth quote is verified verbatim (I re-pulled both podcast transcripts). But the same passage frames Riyadh as *"one of my top three gigs of all fucking time"* and *"that one was a great one,"* inside a run of favorite international gigs — Italy, Germany, Budapest. The draft's private account is a war story told as a highlight with fear inside it, not a confession. Any evaluator can play the episode and hear this.
- **`CLM-32` — the closing beat.** Wikipedia names Burr's *Social Reckoning* character "Charlie"; trade coverage calls him a crisis counselor; a trailer write-up calls him "the only PR guy willing to push back against Zuckerberg's stilted, awkward delivery," with reported dialogue about prepping Zuckerberg for congressional testimony. That reads as crisis *communications*, not the therapeutic reading the final paragraph is built on. The film is unreleased, so nobody can settle it.

